        "original_id": "b7e532f3-b9d5-559a-9fa5-9b21b98c1992",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph Anthony, Anthony Perkins, Shirley MacLaine, Shirley Booth\n- Works: The Matchmaker (1958 film)\n- Organizations: American Film Institute, Kennedy Center Honors\n- Topics: acting awards and honors\n\nFacts:\n- The Matchmaker is a 1958 American comedy film directed by Joseph Anthony.\n- The Matchmaker stars Anthony Perkins, Shirley MacLaine, and Shirley Booth, and it was Shirley Booth's final film.\n- Shirley MacLaine was born Shirley MacLean Beaty on April 24, 1934, and she is an American film, television, and theater actress, singer, dancer, activist, and author.\n- Shirley MacLaine is an Academy Award winner.\n- In 2012, the American Film Institute gave Shirley MacLaine the 40th AFI Life Achievement Award.\n- In 2013, Shirley MacLaine received the Kennedy Center Honors for her lifetime contributions to American culture through the performing arts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
